From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 22:18:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] omarchy-mac: let the J604's carried Chromium decode 10-bit,
 AV1 and HEVC

The J604's own Chromium build (local pkgrel N.6xx) lays out the Apple
Video Decoder's 10-bit (P010) pictures and sizes the decoder's capture
buffers for the renderer, so VP9 profile 2, AV1 and HEVC no longer
stall on its V4L2 decoder. The GPU workaround switches that keep those
codecs in software are only needed for any other Chromium.

Move the browser flags into lib/chromium-flags, which user setup runs
as before. On the J604 it adds the three switches, once each, only when
the installed Chromium is not the carried build, and takes them off
when it is. A chromium pacman hook runs it again after every chromium
install or upgrade for each login account with a Chromium flags file,
so the flags follow a switch between the carried and a stock build. It
is skipped in a chroot and never fails the transaction. Other browsers
and other Macs are unchanged.
---
 omarchy-mac/bin/omarchy-mac-setup-user        | 58 +--------------
 omarchy-mac/lib/chromium-flags                | 73 +++++++++++++++++++
 omarchy-mac/lib/chromium-flags-users          | 15 ++++
 .../91-omarchy-mac-chromium-decoder.hook      | 15 ++++
 omarchy-mac/test/desktop-setup-test.sh        | 55 ++++++++++++++
 5 files changed, 161 insertions(+), 55 deletions(-)
 create mode 100755 omarchy-mac/lib/chromium-flags
 create mode 100755 omarchy-mac/lib/chromium-flags-users
 create mode 100644 omarchy-mac/share/libalpm/hooks/91-omarchy-mac-chromium-decoder.hook

